From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 23:57:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: socinfo: add SM8850P

SoC id 661 is the SM8850P ("CanoeP" in the vendor device tree,
ro.soc.model SM8850P), used in the OnePlus Pad 4. Without a name the
machine attribute of soc0 falls back to the board's model string.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/socinfo.c         | 1 +
 include/dt-bindings/arm/qcom,ids.h | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/socinfo.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/socinfo.c
index 38efc5db7fa8..722a5f511fe7 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/socinfo.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/socinfo.c
@@ -535,6 +535,7 @@ static const struct soc_id soc_id[] = {
 	{ qcom_board_id(QCS6690) },
 	{ qcom_board_id(SM7750) },
 	{ qcom_board_id(SM8850) },
+	{ qcom_board_id(SM8850P) },
 	{ qcom_board_id(IPQ5404) },
 	{ qcom_board_id(QCS9100) },
 	{ qcom_board_id(QCS8300) },
diff --git a/include/dt-bindings/arm/qcom,ids.h b/include/dt-bindings/arm/qcom,ids.h
index 135297027580..a23cbedf62e2 100644
--- a/include/dt-bindings/arm/qcom,ids.h
+++ b/include/dt-bindings/arm/qcom,ids.h
@@ -294,6 +294,7 @@
 #define QCOM_ID_QCS6690			658
 #define QCOM_ID_SM7750			659
 #define QCOM_ID_SM8850			660
+#define QCOM_ID_SM8850P			661
 #define QCOM_ID_IPQ5404			671
 #define QCOM_ID_QCS9100			667
 #define QCOM_ID_QCS8300			674
